menu "Attachments: one brain, many radios (ATTACHMENT-DESIGN)"

config MESHTASTIC_ATTACHMENT_CODEC
	bool
	default y if MESHTASTIC_ATTACHMENT_BRAIN || MESHTASTIC_ATTACHMENT_HEAD || MESHTASTIC_RELAY_EAR
	help
	  The envelope a radio head and its brain exchange (pure byte packing).
	  Pulled in by anything that speaks it; not a user choice.

config MESHTASTIC_ATTACHMENT_BRAIN
	bool "This node is a brain: it hears through radio heads"
	default n
	help
	  Accept attachment envelopes over the BLE peer link. A head's RX_FRAME
	  enters the router as an RF frame tagged with the head's preset and
	  signal; the node's identity, keys, NodeDB and modules stay exactly as
	  they are. Costs a small table (MESHTASTIC_ATTACHMENT_MAX entries) and
	  8 B per RX queue slot; the code is flash.

config MESHTASTIC_ATTACHMENT_MAX
	int "Radio heads a brain tracks (its own radio is not counted)"
	depends on MESHTASTIC_ATTACHMENT_BRAIN
	default 4
	range 1 8
	help
	  A BLE peer link per head; the R8 has 3 connection slots in total.

config MESHTASTIC_ATTACHMENT_HEAD
	bool "This node is a keyless radio head"
	depends on MESHTASTIC_BLE_PEER
	default n
	help
	  (Phase 2.) The radio forwards every frame it hears, undecoded, with its
	  RSSI/SNR and preset, to the brain over the peer link, and transmits
	  frames the brain hands it. The image carries no channel keys, no PKI,
	  no NodeDB and no config beyond its preset and its brain.

endmenu
